# Review ownership for Knap.
#
# One maintainer, so every line names the same person. That looks redundant
# and is not: with branch protection requiring review from a code owner, this
# file is what makes the requirement apply, and the per path entries below
# are what a second maintainer would inherit if one ever appears.
#
# The paths listed separately are the ones where a careless change is
# expensive and the reason is not obvious from the diff. They are not more
# owned than anything else. They are here so that a future rule requiring
# extra review on sensitive paths has somewhere to attach.

# Everything.
*                                   @olaflaitinen

# The encode path. A change here can alter token ids, which breaks every
# consumer that has cached them, and the parity gates are the only thing
# standing between a subtle mistake and a silently wrong tokenizer.
/src/knap/tokenizer.mojo            @olaflaitinen
/src/knap/bpe.mojo                  @olaflaitinen
/src/knap/ranks.mojo                @olaflaitinen
/src/knap/byte_map.mojo             @olaflaitinen
/src/knap/cache.mojo                @olaflaitinen
/src/knap/pretokenize/              @olaflaitinen

# The refusal logic for special tokens. This is the security relevant part of
# the library: a marker in untrusted input that encodes to a control token id
# is prompt injection. See SECURITY.md.
/src/knap/special.mojo              @olaflaitinen

# Generated data. These are not edited by hand, and a hand edit that survives
# review would be reverted by the next generator run, silently.
/src/knap/pretokenize/pattern.mojo  @olaflaitinen
/src/knap/pretokenize/unicode_tables.mojo @olaflaitinen
/scripts/gen_                       @olaflaitinen
/scripts/ucd.py                     @olaflaitinen

# The gates themselves. Weakening one of these is the cheapest way to make
# the whole repository stop meaning anything, and it would not look like much
# in a diff.
/scripts/                           @olaflaitinen
/.github/workflows/                 @olaflaitinen

# The evidence. Changing a published number without changing the run behind
# it is how a benchmark document becomes fiction.
/docs/BENCHMARKS.md                 @olaflaitinen
/docs/CORRECTNESS.md                @olaflaitinen
/bench/results/                     @olaflaitinen
/tests/fuzz/last_run.json           @olaflaitinen
/tests/fuzz/last_run.address.json   @olaflaitinen
